HQBD NOTICE

## Current release: HQBD v0.1.0

HQBD v0.1.0 fuses two external benchmark sources:

1. **CVDP v1.1.0** (872 cases), copied from the HQBD v0.0.1 package under
   `hqbd_v0.1.0/` with v0.1.0 filenames. CVDP case content and case IDs are
   unchanged. See `hqbd_v0.1.0/NOTICE` and `hqbd_v0.0.1/NOTICE` for the
   preserved CVDP notices.
2. **HWE-bench** (417 cases), snapshot 2026-09-09, project
   https://github.com/pku-liang/hwe-bench (Apache-2.0; copy at
   `hqbd_v0.1.0/LICENSE-HWE-bench`), paper arXiv:2604.14709. HWE-bench records
   retain their upstream fields and add HQBD provenance/runnability metadata.

HWE-bench derives from six upstream repositories. Their license verification
status is recorded in `hqbd_v0.1.0/licenses/upstream-repos.md`; licenses are
not asserted where they were not verified. The HWE-bench dataset card declares
Apache-2.0 at the dataset level, and the per-record `license` field is empty for
all 417 records.

Neither CVDP-derived nor HWE-bench-derived content is relicensed as
HQBD-original content. HWE-bench `fix_patch` and `tb_script` are ground-truth
and hidden evaluation material.

## HQBD v0.0.1

HQBD v0.0.1 includes benchmark data from CVDP v1.1.0, repackaged under HQBD v0.0.1 file, directory, and case ID naming for dataset organization.

Source:

Comprehensive Verilog Design Problems (CVDP) Benchmark Dataset
https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/cvdp-benchmark-dataset

Included under `hqbd_v0.0.1/`:

- renamed CVDP JSONL benchmark files for commercial and no_commercial splits;
- renamed CVDP non-agentic code-comprehension JSONL;
- renamed CVDP public agentic-heavy bundle directory as present in the local upstream checkout;
- preserved CVDP `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`, and `CHANGELOG`;
- `ID_MAPPING.csv`, mapping each renamed HQBD case ID to its original CVDP case ID.

CVDP content is not HQBD original content. Third-party notices, source attributions, and license annotations for CVDP are preserved in `hqbd_v0.0.1/NOTICE`.

The JSONL case IDs have been renamed from `cvdp_*` to `hqbd_*`. This renaming is an organizational transformation only. It does not remove or replace the original CVDP attribution, CVDP license terms, or third-party notices.

Heavy bundle filenames and repository references have been renamed from `cvdp_agentic_heavy_*` to `hqbd_agentic_heavy_*` for HQBD organization. Original CVDP bundle filenames are preserved in [BUNDLE_MAPPING.csv](BUNDLE_MAPPING.csv).

## Dataset utility tools

`HQBD/tools/` contains HQBD-adapted helper scripts derived from NVIDIA CVDP benchmark utility tools. The scripts retain their original SPDX copyright and Apache-2.0 license headers.

## Heavy bundle note

The copied CVDP heavy `.bundle` paths may be Git LFS pointer files in the local checkout. A file beginning with `version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1` is not a usable Git bundle. Download and verify real LFS objects before benchmark use or public release of bundle payloads.

## Future HQBD-original content

Future HQBD-original cases should include their own release license and notice terms before public distribution.
